{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"Django works to conform with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG), version 2.2, at the AA level.","source_span":"We work to conform with the `Web Content Accessibility Guidelines`_ (WCAG), version 2.2, at the AA level."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"WCAG is described as the most established standard for web accessibility, and AA-level guidelines are the most common legal compliance target worldwide.","source_span":"WCAG is the most established standard for web accessibility. `AA-level guidelines`_ are the most common legal compliance target worldwide."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"Beyond AA, Django also aims to follow WCAG 2.2 AAA-level guidelines, the upcoming WCAG 3.0 standard, and Authoring Tool Accessibility Guidelines (ATAG) 2.0.","source_span":"WCAG 2.2 `AAA-level guidelines`_ – stricter criteria that go beyond the AA level... The upcoming `WCAG 3.0`_ guidelines... `Authoring Tool Accessibility Guidelines`_ (ATAG) 2.0"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"Django's Accessibility team can be reached via the Accessibility Django forum topic or the #accessibility channel on the Django Discord server.","source_span":"You can reach out to the `Accessibility team`_ via the `Accessibility Django forum topic`_ or via the ``#accessibility`` channel on the `Django Discord server`_."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"UI changes should always be tested with keyboard-only navigation and the Accessibility Insights browser extension's automated checks feature (or an equivalent tool with the Axe checker).","source_span":"Always test user interface changes with:\n\n* Keyboard-only navigation... * The `Accessibility Insights`_ browser extension's automated checks feature, or an equivalent tool with the `Axe`_ checker."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"Where UI changes could affect other modalities, testing should also include touch-only navigation, 400% browser zoom, and forced-colors mode.","source_span":"Where the UI changes could affect those modalities, also test with:\n\n* Touch-only navigation... * 400% browser zoom... * Forced-colors mode"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"Forced-colors mode can be tested via the \"high_contrast\" mode in the screenshot tests.","source_span":"Note that this can be tested via the ``\"high_contrast\"`` mode in the :ref:`screenshot tests <screenshot-tests>`."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"For Windows, Django recommends testing with NVDA (with Firefox ESR), Narrator (with Microsoft Edge), Windows Magnifier, Windows Speech Recognition, and Contrast themes.","source_span":"For Windows:\n\n* `NVDA`_ - recommended with Firefox ESR\n* `Narrator`_ - recommended with Microsoft Edge\n* Windows Magnifier\n* Windows Speech Recognition\n* `Contrast themes`_"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"For macOS, Django recommends testing with VoiceOver (with Safari), macOS Zoom, and macOS Voice Control.","source_span":"For macOS:\n\n* `VoiceOver`_ - recommended with Safari\n* macOS Zoom\n* macOS Voice Control"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"For Linux, Django recommends testing with Orca, recommended with Firefox ESR.","source_span":"For Linux:\n\n* `Orca`_ - recommended with Firefox ESR"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"For mobile or tablet, Django recommends testing with VoiceOver on iOS or TalkBack on Android.","source_span":"For mobile or tablet:\n\n* VoiceOver on iOS, or TalkBack on Android"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","statement":"Django also recommends testing with popular licensed assistive technologies JAWS and Dragon, both on Windows, if a user or license is available.","source_span":"also test against:\n\n* `JAWS`_ on Windows\n* `Dragon`_ on Windows"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","fact_refs":[0],"question":"At what WCAG version and conformance level does Django aim to comply for accessibility?","answer":"Django aims to conform with WCAG version 2.2 at the AA level."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","fact_refs":[7],"question":"Which screen reader does Django recommend for testing on Windows, and which browser should it be paired with?","answer":"NVDA is recommended with Firefox ESR (Narrator is also recommended, paired with Microsoft Edge)."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","fact_refs":[8],"question":"Which screen reader does Django recommend for testing on macOS, and which browser?","answer":"VoiceOver, recommended with Safari."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_django_accessibility","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What automated tool does Django recommend for accessibility checks during UI testing?","answer":"The Accessibility Insights browser extension's automated checks feature, or an equivalent tool with the Axe checker."}
